{
  "$comment": [
    "#1633 - the bytes iOS puts on the wire for every at-risk request body.",
    "",
    "GENERATED, not hand-written: apps/ios/Tests/Unit/APIServiceWireFormatTests.swift",
    "(testCommittedFixtureMatchesWhatWeActuallySend) encodes each body through the real",
    "APIService request path and fails if the 'bodies' object below does not match,",
    "printing the observed bytes between markers so they can be copied in.",
    "",
    "'wire' is what iOS sends today. 'legacySnakeCase' is what it sent while APIService",
    "set .convertToSnakeCase on the shared encoder - produced by the same JSONEncoder",
    "with that strategy restored, so it is the historic bytes, not a reconstruction.",
    "",
    "Note what 'legacySnakeCase' does and does not convert, because it is not what you",
    "would guess and it was measured, not assumed: the strategy rewrites a type's own",
    "CodingKeys, and the keys of a TOP-LEVEL Dictionary body (APIService wraps every body",
    "in AnyEncodable, which erases the type, and Foundation only skips conversion for a",
    "Dictionary it can see statically - compare storeUserRecoveryEnvelope's hub_id). It",
    "does NOT touch the keys of a NESTED Dictionary - see createContact, where",
    "blindIndexes becomes blind_indexes while the nameToken inside it is untouched.",
    "",
    "apps/worker/__tests__/unit/ios-wire-bodies.test.ts round-trips both through the real",
    "Zod schemas: 'wire' must validate with every key intact, and 'legacySnakeCase' must",
    "either be rejected (the loud failures) or validate having silently lost the",
    "ciphertext and envelope keys (the data-loss set). Neither side can drift from the",
    "other, and neither can drift from the contract."
  ],
